      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the formatting fixes. I think we can land this, according to the general Chromium policy for external architecture-specific contributions. We do need a second reviewer for external contributions, so I\u0027m adding Herb.\n\nAs with other chromium projects, we don\u0027t make any promises about maintenance of this code - it may break at some point. I do want to add a compile job, when we have time, to ensure the code stays healthy. Our infrastructure team is very busy right now, so it might not happen immediately.\n\nOne question: Does the loongarch backend have problems with no-lax-vector-conversion, or is it just that you didn\u0027t write the code to do the necessary casts? (I know that we enforced that flag after you started writing this CL).",
      "revId": "c377e73a56a4214ebaa6c3fbcef28258eaef8450",
